  {"term_id": "Ta'dil", "def_id": "Penilaian adil terhadap seorang perawi, yang menyatakan bahwa perawi tersebut terpercaya dan dapat diterima riwayatnya.", "def_en": "Validation or declaration of a narrator as just, reliable, and trustworthy.", "id": "tadil", "term_en": "Ta'dil"},
  {"id": "arbain_nawawi", "term_en": "Forty Hadith of an-Nawawi", "term_id": "Hadits Arba'in An-Nawawi", "def_en": "An-Nawawi's selection of 42 hadiths, each treated as one principle of the religion, from intention and revelation to creed, law and character. The title says forty, but the book holds 42.", "def_id": "Kumpulan 42 hadits pilihan Imam an-Nawawi, masing-masing dianggap satu prinsip agama, dari niat dan wahyu sampai akidah, hukum, dan akhlak. Judulnya menyebut empat puluh, tetapi kitabnya memuat 42 hadits."},
  {"id": "qudsi_40", "term_en": "40 Hadith Qudsi", "term_id": "40 Hadits Qudsi", "def_en": "A short reader of 40 hadiths in which the Prophet reports the words of Allah. They are not Quran and are not recited as Quran, and their chains are graded like any other hadith.", "def_id": "Bacaan ringkas berisi 40 hadits yang di dalamnya Nabi SAW menyampaikan firman Allah. Hadits ini bukan Al-Qur'an dan tidak dibaca sebagai Al-Qur'an, serta sanadnya dinilai seperti hadits lain."},
  {"id": "arbain_shah_waliullah", "term_en": "Forty Hadith of Shah Waliullah", "term_id": "40 Hadits Shah Waliullah", "def_en": "A forty-hadith selection by Shah Waliullah ad-Dihlawi (d. 1176 AH), each hadith chosen as a summary of one major principle of the religion.", "def_id": "Kumpulan empat puluh hadits pilihan Shah Waliullah ad-Dihlawi (wafat 1176 H), setiap hadits mewakili satu prinsip besar dalam agama."},
  {"id": "adab_mufrad", "term_en": "Al-Adab al-Mufrad", "term_id": "Al-Adab Al-Mufrad", "def_en": "Al-Bukhari's separate collection on manners and character, with over 1,300 narrations on parents, neighbours, speech, eating and conduct. It is a companion to his Sahih, not a part of it.", "def_id": "Koleksi tersendiri Imam al-Bukhari tentang adab dan akhlak, memuat lebih dari 1.300 riwayat tentang orang tua, tetangga, ucapan, makan, dan pergaulan. Kitab ini pelengkap Shahih-nya, bukan bagian dari Shahih."},
  {"id": "bulugh_maram", "term_en": "Bulugh al-Maram", "term_id": "Bulughul Maram", "def_en": "Ibn Hajar al-'Asqalani's selection of legal hadiths, with the source of each hadith named in the text itself (takhrij). It is a standard study text in Southeast Asian pesantren, usually read together with Subul as-Salam.", "def_id": "Kumpulan hadits-hadits hukum pilihan Ibnu Hajar al-'Asqalani, dengan sumber setiap hadits disebutkan langsung dalam teks (takhrij). Menjadi kitab kajian baku di pesantren Nusantara, biasanya dibaca bersama Subulus Salam."},
  {"id": "mishkat_masabih", "term_en": "Mishkat al-Masabih", "term_id": "Misykat al-Mashabih", "def_en": "Al-Khatib at-Tabrizi's expansion of Masabih as-Sunna: he adds the chain and usually a grade to each hadith, which made it a graded anthology of the Prophet's teaching across creed, worship and conduct.", "def_id": "Perluasan Masabihus Sunnah oleh al-Khathib at-Tabrizi: ia menambahkan sanad dan biasanya derajat hadits pada tiap riwayat, sehingga kitab ini menjadi bunga rampai hadits berderajat yang mencakup akidah, ibadah, dan adab."},
  {"id": "riyad_salihin", "term_en": "Riyad as-Salihin", "term_id": "Riyadhus Shalihin", "def_en": "An-Nawawi's thematic anthology of about 1,900 hadiths on virtues, worship and daily conduct, arranged as chapters of encouragement rather than as a legal manual.", "def_id": "Bunga rampai tematik Imam an-Nawawi berisi sekitar 1.900 hadits tentang keutamaan amal, ibadah, dan adab keseharian, disusun sebagai bab-bab penyemangat, bukan kitab hukum."},
  {"id": "shamail_muhammadiyah", "term_en": "Shamail al-Muhammadiyah", "term_id": "Syamail Muhammadiyah", "def_en": "At-Tirmidhi's collection of about 400 narrations describing the Prophet's body, hair, clothing, food, speech and laughter — a portrait of his person rather than his rulings.", "def_id": "Koleksi at-Tirmidzi berisi sekitar 400 riwayat tentang fisik, rambut, pakaian, makanan, tutur kata, dan canda Nabi SAW — potret pribadi beliau, bukan kitab hukum."},
  {"id": "mujam_kabir", "term_en": "Al-Mu'jam al-Kabir", "term_id": "Mu'jam al-Kabir", "def_en": "At-Tabarani's largest mu'jam, arranged by Companion and then by the narrators around each one. It preserves thousands of narrations absent from the six books, and many Companions have a section of their own.", "def_id": "Mu'jam terbesar at-Thabarani, disusun menurut nama sahabat lalu menurut perawi di sekitarnya. Kitab ini menyimpan ribuan riwayat yang tidak ada dalam Kutubus Sittah, dan banyak sahabat memiliki bagian tersendiri."},
  {"id": "musnad_syafii", "term_en": "Musnad al-Shafi'i", "term_id": "Musnad Syafi'i", "def_en": "Hadiths transmitted through Imam ash-Shafi'i (d. 204 AH), arranged by chain. Scholars note that this musnad was gathered from his transmissions after him, so the arrangement is later than the imam himself.", "def_id": "Hadits-hadits yang diriwayatkan melalui Imam asy-Syafi'i (wafat 204 H), disusun menurut sanad. Para ulama mencatat bahwa musnad ini dihimpun dari riwayat-riwayat beliau setelah wafatnya, sehingga penyusunannya lebih belakangan."},
  {"id": "sahih_ibn_khuzaimah", "term_en": "Sahih Ibn Khuzaimah", "term_id": "Shahih Ibnu Khuzaimah", "def_en": "Ibn Khuzaimah's (d. 311 AH) collection limited to hadiths he judged authentic with a continuous chain. Scholars cite it beside the two Sahihs when grading a hadith.", "def_id": "Koleksi Ibnu Khuzaimah (wafat 311 H) yang hanya memuat hadits yang ia nilai sahih dengan sanad bersambung. Kitab ini dijadikan rujukan penilaian hadits di samping dua Shahih."},
  {"id": "sahih_ibn_hibban", "term_en": "Sahih Ibn Hibban", "term_id": "Shahih Ibnu Hibban", "def_en": "Ibn Hibban's (d. 354 AH) collection of what he considered authentic, arranged by types (taqasim) instead of fiqh chapters. Its standard is looser than the two Sahihs, so later scholars re-examined many of its hadiths.", "def_id": "Koleksi Ibnu Hibban (wafat 354 H) atas hadits yang ia nilai sahih, disusun menurut jenis (taqasim), bukan bab fikih. Standarnya lebih longgar daripada dua Shahih, sehingga banyak haditsnya ditinjau ulang ulama sesudahnya."},
  {"id": "mustadrak_hakim", "term_en": "Al-Mustadrak 'ala as-Sahihayn", "term_id": "Al-Mustadrak al-Hakim", "def_en": "Al-Hakim an-Naisaburi's (d. 405 AH) supplement gathering hadiths that meet al-Bukhari's and Muslim's conditions but were left out of their books. Its grades are disputed, and adh-Dhahabi reviewed them in his Talkhis.", "def_id": "Suplemen al-Hakim an-Naisaburi (wafat 405 H) yang menghimpun hadits sesuai syarat al-Bukhari dan Muslim namun tidak dimuat dalam kedua kitab itu. Penilaiannya diperdebatkan, dan adz-Dzahabi meninjaunya dalam Talkhish-nya."},
  {"id": "sunan_daruquthni", "term_en": "Sunan ad-Daruquthni", "term_id": "Sunan Ad-Daruquthni", "def_en": "Ad-Daruquthni's (d. 385 AH) collection of legal hadiths with close attention to hidden defects ('ilal) and to the chains jurists actually relied on.", "def_id": "Kumpulan hadits hukum ad-Daruquthni (wafat 385 H) dengan perhatian besar pada cacat tersembunyi ('ilal) dan pada sanad yang benar-benar dipakai para ahli fikih."},
  {"id": "muntaqa_akhbar", "term_en": "Muntaqa al-Akhbar", "term_id": "Muntaqa al-Akhbar", "def_en": "A selection of legal hadiths by Majd ad-Din Ibn Taymiyyah, grandfather of Taqi ad-Din Ibn Taymiyyah. Ash-Shawkani's commentary Nayl al-Awtar made it a standard comparative fiqh reference.", "def_id": "Kumpulan hadits hukum pilihan Majduddin Ibnu Taimiyah, kakek dari Taqiyuddin Ibnu Taimiyah. Karena syarah Nailul Authar karya asy-Syaukani, kitab ini menjadi rujukan fikih perbandingan yang baku."},
  {"id": "maani_athar", "term_en": "Ma'ani al-Athar", "term_id": "Ma'ani al-Atsar", "def_en": "At-Tahawi's (d. 321 AH) Hanafi work that gathers hadiths topic by topic and reconciles narrations that look contradictory — a key text for how jurists read hadith.", "def_id": "Karya at-Thahawi (wafat 321 H) bermazhab Hanafi yang menghimpun hadits per topik dan mendamaikan riwayat-riwayat yang tampak bertentangan — rujukan penting untuk memahami cara ahli fikih membaca hadits."},
  {"id": "masabih_sunna", "term_en": "Masabih as-Sunna", "term_id": "Masabihus Sunnah", "def_en": "Al-Baghawi's (d. 516 AH) topic-ordered selection of authenticated and well-known hadiths, given without chains. Al-Khatib at-Tabrizi later expanded it into Mishkat al-Masabih.", "def_id": "Kumpulan hadits pilihan al-Baghawi (wafat 516 H) yang sahih dan masyhur, disusun per topik tanpa menyebut sanad. Al-Khathib at-Tabrizi kemudian memperluasnya menjadi Misykat al-Mashabih."},
  {"id": "umdat_ahkam", "term_en": "Umdat al-Ahkam", "term_id": "Umdatul Ahkam", "def_en": "Ibn Daqiq al-'Id's (d. 702 AH) compact collection of the legal hadiths that al-Bukhari and Muslim agreed upon, about 400 in number, widely used as a first fiqh-hadith text.", "def_id": "Kumpulan ringkas hadits hukum yang disepakati al-Bukhari dan Muslim, sekitar 400 hadits, disusun Ibnu Daqiq al-'Id (wafat 702 H) dan luas dipakai sebagai kitab awal belajar hadits hukum."},
  {"id": "fath_al_bari", "term_en": "Fath al-Bari", "term_id": "Fathul Bari", "def_en": "Ibn Hajar al-'Asqalani's (d. 852 AH) commentary on Sahih al-Bukhari, the most detailed sharh of that collection: it works through wording, grammar, chains, narrator biography and legal rulings.", "def_id": "Syarah Shahih al-Bukhari karya Ibnu Hajar al-'Asqalani (wafat 852 H), syarah paling luas atas kitab itu: membahas lafaz, tata bahasa, sanad, biografi perawi, dan hukum."},
  {"id": "syarh_nawawi_muslim", "term_en": "Syarh an-Nawawi 'ala Muslim", "term_id": "Syarah Nawawi atas Muslim", "def_en": "An-Nawawi's (d. 676 AH) commentary on Sahih Muslim, known as al-Minhaj: the standard companion for wording, chains and legal meaning, and the reference for how Muslim's chapters are read.", "def_id": "Syarah Shahih Muslim karya an-Nawawi (wafat 676 H) yang dikenal sebagai al-Minhaj: pendamping baku untuk lafaz, sanad, dan makna hukum, sekaligus rujukan cara membaca bab-bab dalam Shahih Muslim."},
  {"id": "awn_al_mabud", "term_en": "'Awn al-Ma'bud", "term_id": "'Aunul Ma'bud", "def_en": "Shams al-Haqq al-'Azimabadi's (d. 1329 AH) commentary on Sunan Abi Dawud, usually printed together with Ibn al-Qayyim's Tahdhib as-Sunan.", "def_id": "Syarah Sunan Abu Dawud karya Syamsul Haq al-'Azhimabadi (wafat 1329 H), biasanya dicetak bersama Tahdzibus Sunan karya Ibnul Qayyim."},
  {"id": "tuhfat_al_ahwadhi", "term_en": "Tuhfat al-Ahwadhi", "term_id": "Tuhfatul Ahwadzi", "def_en": "Abd ar-Rahman al-Mubarakpuri's (d. 1353 AH) commentary on Jami' at-Tirmidhi, explaining the wording, the chains and the grades at-Tirmidhi attached to each hadith.", "def_id": "Syarah Jami' at-Tirmidzi karya Abdurrahman al-Mubarakfuri (wafat 1353 H), menjelaskan lafaz, sanad, dan derajat hadits yang dicantumkan at-Tirmidzi."},
  {"id": "mirqat_al_mafatih", "term_en": "Mirqat al-Mafatih", "term_id": "Mirqatul Mafatih", "def_en": "Mulla 'Ali al-Qari's (d. 1014 AH) large commentary on Mishkat al-Masabih, strong on wording, hadith grades and Hanafi legal reading.", "def_id": "Syarah besar atas Misykat al-Mashabih karya Mulla Ali al-Qari (wafat 1014 H), kuat dalam pembahasan lafaz, derajat hadits, dan pembacaan hukum mazhab Hanafi."},
  {"id": "nayl_al_awtar", "term_en": "Nayl al-Awtar", "term_id": "Nailul Authar", "def_en": "Ash-Shawkani's (d. 1250 AH) commentary on Muntaqa al-Akhbar, setting each hadith against the positions of the legal schools. It is a standard comparative fiqh reference.", "def_id": "Syarah Muntaqa al-Akhbar karya asy-Syaukani (wafat 1250 H) yang membandingkan tiap hadits dengan pendapat mazhab-mazhab fikih. Menjadi rujukan baku fikih perbandingan."},
  {"id": "subul_as_salam", "term_en": "Subul as-Salam", "term_id": "Subulus Salam", "def_en": "As-San'ani's (d. 1182 AH) commentary on Bulugh al-Maram, explaining the legal point of each hadith and discussing its grade.", "def_id": "Syarah Bulughul Maram karya as-San'ani (wafat 1182 H), menjelaskan sisi hukum tiap hadits dan membahas derajatnya."},
  {"id": "tamhid_ibn_abdilbarr", "term_en": "At-Tamhid", "term_id": "At-Tamhid", "def_en": "Ibn 'Abd al-Barr's (d. 463 AH) study of the chains and meanings in Muwatta Malik, one of the earliest systematic works of isnad analysis.", "def_id": "Kajian Ibnu Abdil Barr (wafat 463 H) atas sanad dan makna dalam Muwaththa' Malik, salah satu karya analisis sanad paling awal yang sistematis."},
  {"id": "jami_ulum_hikam", "term_en": "Jami' al-'Ulum wa al-Hikam", "term_id": "Jami'ul Ulum wal Hikam", "def_en": "Ibn Rajab al-Hanbali's (d. 795 AH) commentary on an-Nawawi's Forty Hadith, expanded to fifty hadiths, treating each one as a principle of the religion.", "def_id": "Syarah atas Hadits Arba'in an-Nawawi karya Ibnu Rajab al-Hanbali (wafat 795 H), diperluas menjadi lima puluh hadits, dan setiap hadits dibahas sebagai satu prinsip agama."},
  {"id": "ihkam_al_ahkam", "term_en": "Ihkam al-Ahkam", "term_id": "Ihkamul Ahkam", "def_en": "Ibn Daqiq al-'Id's own commentary on Umdat al-Ahkam, working out the legal rulings from the hadiths agreed upon by the two Sahihs.", "def_id": "Syarah Umdatul Ahkam karya penulisnya sendiri, Ibnu Daqiq al-'Id, yang menggali hukum-hukum dari hadits yang disepakati dua Shahih."},
  {"id": "kutub_sittah", "term_en": "Kutub al-Sittah", "term_id": "Kutubus Sittah", "def_en": "The six canonical Sunni collections: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abi Dawud, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i and Sunan Ibn Majah. Some scholars count the Muwatta of Malik or Sunan ad-Darimi in place of Ibn Majah, so the six are a convention rather than a fixed list.", "def_id": "Enam kitab induk dalam tradisi Sunni: Shahih al-Bukhari, Shahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawud, Jami' at-Tirmidzi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, dan Sunan Ibnu Majah. Sebagian ulama menukar Ibnu Majah dengan Muwaththa' Malik atau Sunan ad-Darimi, sehingga enam kitab ini adalah kesepakatan umum, bukan daftar yang mutlak."},
  {"id": "sahihayn", "term_en": "As-Sahihayn", "term_id": "Ash-Shahihain", "def_en": "The two collections held most authentic after the Quran, Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim. A hadith found in both is called muttafaqun 'alaih.", "def_id": "Dua kitab yang dianggap paling sahih setelah Al-Qur'an, yaitu Shahih al-Bukhari dan Shahih Muslim. Hadits yang termuat di keduanya disebut muttafaqun 'alaih."},
  {"id": "penomoran_hadits", "term_en": "Hadith Numbering", "term_id": "Penomoran Hadits", "def_en": "The number a hadith carries depends on the edition and the database: a printed copy, an abridgement and a digital corpus each count chapters and repetitions differently, so the same hadith can hold several numbers. This site numbers every collection separately and never mixes numbers across datasets.", "def_id": "Nomor sebuah hadits bergantung pada edisi dan basis datanya: cetakan, ringkasan, dan korpus digital menghitung bab serta pengulangan secara berbeda, sehingga satu hadits bisa punya beberapa nomor. Situs ini menomori setiap kitab secara terpisah dan tidak mencampur nomor antar kumpulan data."},
  {"id": "tahqiq", "term_en": "Tahqiq (Critical Edition)", "term_id": "Tahqiq (Edisi Kritis)", "def_en": "The scholarly work of establishing a reliable text of a book by comparing its manuscripts, recording variants and verifying citations. The editor is called a muhaqqiq, and different editions of one collection can differ in both text and numbering.", "def_id": "Upaya ilmiah menetapkan teks kitab yang paling mendekati aslinya dengan membandingkan naskah-naskah, mencatat perbedaan, dan memverifikasi kutipan. Penyuntingnya disebut muhaqqiq, dan edisi berbeda dari satu kitab bisa berbeda teks maupun penomorannya."},
  {"id": "mukhtasar", "term_en": "Mukhtasar", "term_id": "Mukhtashar", "def_en": "An abridgement of a larger work: repeated chains, weak narrations or long commentary are dropped while the subject matter is kept.", "def_id": "Ringkasan dari kitab yang lebih besar: sanad yang berulang, hadits lemah, atau uraian panjang dibuang, sementara pokok bahasannya dipertahankan."},
  {"id": "maqtu", "term_en": "Maqtu'", "term_id": "Maqthu'", "def_en": "A statement or action attributed to a Successor (Tabi'i), stopping before the Companion and the Prophet. It records early community practice rather than a saying of the Prophet.", "def_id": "Ucapan atau perbuatan yang disandarkan kepada Tabi'in, terhenti pada Tabi'in dan tidak sampai kepada sahabat maupun Nabi SAW. Riwayat ini mencatat praktik generasi awal, bukan sabda Nabi."},
  {"id": "mudraj", "term_en": "Mudraj", "term_id": "Mudraj", "def_en": "A hadith whose text contains an insertion: a narrator's own words or explanation were folded into the Prophet's wording without a clear break.", "def_id": "Hadits yang dalam matannya tersisip kata-kata perawi, berupa penjelasan atau tambahan, tanpa pemisah yang jelas, sehingga seolah-olah bagian dari sabda Nabi SAW."},
  {"id": "mudtarib", "term_en": "Mudtarib", "term_id": "Mudhtharib", "def_en": "A hadith transmitted in conflicting versions of equal strength, where no version can be preferred over the others and the conflict cannot be reconciled.", "def_id": "Hadits yang diriwayatkan dalam versi-versi yang saling bertentangan dengan kekuatan seimbang, sehingga tidak ada versi yang bisa diunggulkan dan pertentangannya tidak dapat didamaikan."},
  {"id": "maqlub", "term_en": "Maqlub", "term_id": "Maqlub", "def_en": "A hadith whose chain or text has been inverted: a narrator's name swapped for another, or the text of one hadith attached to the chain of another.", "def_id": "Hadits yang sanad atau matannya tertukar: nama perawi ditukar dengan perawi lain, atau matan suatu hadits dipasang pada sanad hadits lain."},
  {"id": "mutabi_shahid", "term_en": "Mutabi' and Shahid", "term_id": "Mutabi' dan Syahid", "def_en": "Two kinds of corroboration. A mutabi' is another chain from the same level supporting a narrator; a shahid is a hadith from a different Companion supporting the same meaning. Either can lift a weak hadith toward hasan.", "def_id": "Dua bentuk penguat riwayat. Mutabi' adalah sanad lain dari tingkatan yang sama yang menguatkan seorang perawi; syahid adalah hadits dari sahabat lain yang menguatkan makna yang sama. Keduanya dapat menaikkan hadits lemah ke arah hasan."},
  {"id": "illah", "term_en": "'Illah (Hidden Defect)", "term_id": "'Illah (Cacat Tersembunyi)", "def_en": "A subtle defect in a chain that looks sound — an inserted narrator, a wrong attribution, a hidden break — visible only after comparing many chains. The science of 'ilal is the hardest part of hadith criticism.", "def_id": "Cacat halus pada sanad yang tampak sahih — perawi yang disisipkan, penyandaran yang keliru, atau keterputusan yang tersembunyi — yang baru tampak setelah membandingkan banyak sanad. Ilmu 'ilal adalah bagian tersulit dalam kritik hadits."},
  {"id": "tabaqat", "term_en": "Tabaqat (Generations)", "term_id": "Thabaqat (Tingkatan)", "def_en": "The layers of narrators by generation, from the Companions down to the later compilers. Placing two narrators in the same tabaqat is how scholars test whether a chain could really have met.", "def_id": "Lapisan perawi menurut generasi, dari para sahabat hingga para penyusun kitab belakangan. Penentuan thabaqat dipakai ulama untuk menguji apakah suatu sanad benar-benar memungkinkan terjadinya pertemuan."},
  {"id": "kunyah", "term_en": "Kunyah", "term_id": "Kunyah", "def_en": "An honorific name-form built on Abu (father of) or Umm (mother of), such as Abu Hurayrah. Narrators are often listed by kunyah, so one person can appear under both a kunyah and a given name.", "def_id": "Bentuk nama kehormatan dengan Abu (bapak dari) atau Umm (ibu dari), seperti Abu Hurairah. Perawi sering dicatat dengan kunyah, sehingga satu orang bisa muncul dalam bentuk kunyah maupun nama aslinya."},
  {"id": "nisbah", "term_en": "Nisbah", "term_id": "Nisbah", "def_en": "The part of a name tying a person to a place, tribe, trade or school: al-Bukhari (Bukhara), an-Naisaburi (Nishapur), al-Hanafi. It helps identify a narrator and hints at generation and teachers.", "def_id": "Bagian nama yang menghubungkan seseorang dengan tempat, kabilah, profesi, atau mazhab: al-Bukhari (Bukhara), an-Naisaburi (Naisabur), al-Hanafi. Nisbah membantu mengenali perawi dan memberi petunjuk tentang generasi serta gurunya."},
  {"id": "riwayah_dirayah", "term_en": "Riwayah and Dirayah", "term_id": "Riwayah dan Dirayah", "def_en": "The two branches of hadith science. Riwayah is the accurate transmission of the text from teacher to student; dirayah is the critical study of chain and text — who is reliable, where the chain breaks, what the wording means.", "def_id": "Dua cabang ilmu hadits. Riwayah adalah penyampaian teks secara akurat dari guru ke murid; dirayah adalah kajian kritis atas sanad dan matan — siapa yang terpercaya, di mana sanad terputus, dan apa makna redaksinya."},
  {"id": "tadlis", "term_en": "Tadlis", "term_id": "Tadlis", "def_en": "Concealing a weak point in the chain, most often dropping a weak teacher's name and replacing 'heard from' with a vague 'from' so the chain looks continuous. The resulting hadith is called mudallas.", "def_id": "Menyembunyikan kelemahan dalam sanad, umumnya dengan menghapus nama guru yang lemah dan mengganti lafaz 'mendengar dari' menjadi 'dari' yang samar agar sanad tampak bersambung. Hadits hasilnya disebut mudallas."},
  {"id": "zawaid", "term_en": "Zawa'id", "term_id": "Zawa'id", "def_en": "The narrations a compiler carries beyond the book he is supplementing — for example the zawa'id of Musnad Ahmad over the six books. Zawa'id works are how the unique material of a collection is located and graded.", "def_id": "Riwayat yang dibawa seorang penyusun di luar kitab yang menjadi sumbernya — misalnya zawa'id Musnad Ahmad terhadap Kutubus Sittah. Kitab zawa'id dipakai untuk menemukan dan menilai hadits yang khas pada satu kitab."},
  {"id": "taraf", "term_en": "Taraf", "term_id": "Tharaf", "def_en": "The opening phrase of a hadith, used as its index key. Reference works called atraf list a hadith by its first words and then gather every chain and source that carries it.", "def_id": "Potongan awal sebuah hadits yang dipakai sebagai kunci indeks. Kitab yang disebut athraf mendaftar hadits berdasarkan lafaz awalnya, lalu mengumpulkan seluruh sanad dan sumber yang memuatnya."},
  {"id": "musalsal", "term_en": "Musalsal", "term_id": "Musalsal", "def_en": "A hadith whose chain carries a repeated feature at every level — all narrators from one city, all using the same phrase, or all narrating with a set gesture.", "def_id": "Hadits yang sanadnya memiliki ciri berulang pada setiap tingkatan — semua perawi dari satu kota, semua memakai lafal yang sama, atau semua meriwayatkan dengan gerakan tertentu."},
  {"id": "ikhtilat", "term_en": "Ikhtilat", "term_id": "Ikhtilat", "def_en": "A decline in a narrator's memory late in life. What he narrated before the change is accepted; what he narrated afterwards, or what was heard from him then, is treated with caution.", "def_id": "Melemahnya hafalan seorang perawi di usia lanjut atau setelah peristiwa tertentu. Riwayat sebelum perubahan itu diterima; riwayat sesudahnya, atau riwayat yang didengar pada masa itu, diperlakukan dengan hati-hati."},
  {"id": "sahih_li_ghairihi", "term_en": "Sahih and Hasan li-Ghairihi", "term_id": "Shahih dan Hasan Lighairihi", "def_en": "Grades raised by corroboration. A hasan hadith with several supporting chains becomes sahih li-ghairihi; a weak hadith with support but a softer narrator becomes hasan li-ghairihi. The original weakness is compensated, not erased.", "def_id": "Derajat yang naik karena adanya penguat. Hadits hasan dengan beberapa sanad pendukung menjadi sahih lighairihi; hadits lemah yang punya penguat namun perawinya kurang kuat menjadi hasan lighairihi. Kelemahan asalnya tertutup oleh penguat, bukan hilang."},
  {"id": "shighah_tahammul", "term_en": "Transmission Formulas", "term_id": "Lafal Periwayatan", "def_en": "The words showing how a narrator received a hadith: haddathana and akhbarana (he told us) point to direct hearing, 'an (from) can hide a gap, and 'an'anah — a chain of bare 'from' links — is accepted only under conditions.", "def_id": "Lafal yang menunjukkan cara perawi menerima hadits: haddatsana dan akhbarana (telah menyampaikan kepada kami) menandakan pendengaran langsung, 'an (dari) dapat menyembunyikan keterputusan, dan 'an'anah — sanad yang seluruhnya memakai 'dari' — hanya diterima dengan syarat tertentu."},
  {"id": "adl", "term_en": "'Adl (Integrity)", "term_id": "'Adl (Keadilan Perawi)", "def_en": "The first half of trustworthiness: a narrator is Muslim, sane, adult, free of open major sin and of anything that damages honour. Paired with dabit, it makes a narrator tsiqah.", "def_id": "Separuh pertama syarat kepercayaan perawi: Muslim, berakal, balig, tidak melakukan dosa besar secara terbuka, dan terhindar dari hal yang merusak muru'ah. Bila dipasangkan dengan dhabit, perawi disebut tsiqah."},
